{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV5voiceAA8MXLVoiceVSgvp","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"voice","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLVoice","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLVoiceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","title":"voice","symbolKind":"property"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"voice"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLVoice","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLVoiceV","text":"MXLVoice"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<voice>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/voice"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/voice","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A voice is a sequence of musical events (e.g. notes, chords, rests) that proceeds linearly in time. The voice","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element is used to distinguish between multiple voices in individual parts. It is defined within a group due"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","title":"MXLNote","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/voice":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/voice","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/voice","abstract":[{"text":"A voice is a sequence of musical events (e.g. notes, chords, rests) that proceeds linearly in time. The voice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element is used to distinguish between multiple voices in individual parts. It is defined within a group due","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"title":"voice","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"voice","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLVoice","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLVoiceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLVoice":{"abstract":[{"text":"A voice is a sequence of musical events (e.g. notes, chords, rests) that proceeds linearly in time. The voice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element is used to distinguish between multiple voices in individual parts. It is defined within a group due","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLVoice","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"MXLVoice","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLVoice","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvoice","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLVoice"}}}